## Sensible Starting Values

```xiom
pub interface Default {
  fn default() -> Self;
}
```

### Implementing Default

```xiom
pub type Config = {
  host: Str;
  port: Int;
  retries: Int;
}

impl Default for Config {
  fn default() -> Config {
    return Config{
      host: "localhost",
      port: 8080,
      retries: 3,
    };
  }
}

fn main() {
  let config = Config::default();
  // Start with defaults, override what you need
  let mut custom = Config::default();
  custom.port = 3000;
}
```

### Default with Collections

```xiom
let nums = HashMap[Str, Vec[Int]]();
// Vec::default() is called automatically for missing keys
nums.entry("even").or_default().push(2);
nums.entry("even").or_default().push(4);
```

### Zero Values

```xiom
impl Default for Int { fn default() -> Int { return 0; } }
impl Default for Bool { fn default() -> Bool { return false; } }
impl Default for Str { fn default() -> Str { return ""; } }
impl Default for Vec[T] { fn default() -> Vec[T] { return Vec[T](); } }
impl Default for Option[T] { fn default() -> Option[T] { return None(); } }
```

### Builder Pattern with Default

```xiom
fn create_config() -> Config {
  var c = Config::default();
  c.host = get_env("HOST").unwrap_or("0.0.0.0");
  c.port = get_env("PORT").unwrap_or(8080);
  return c;
}
```

